{
  "name": "OpenShorts: video URL in, published-ready clips out (no polling)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## OpenShorts + n8n, the whole loop\n\n**One HTTP request starts the job, one signed webhook ends it.** No polling loop, no wait nodes.\n\n### Setup (3 steps)\n1. Create an API key at [openshorts.app](https://www.openshorts.app/) (account page, starts with `osk_`). Add a **Header Auth** credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer osk_...`, and select it in the *Start OpenShorts job* node.\n2. Open the *Clips ready* webhook node, copy its **production** URL, and paste it as `webhook_url` in the *Start OpenShorts job* node body.\n3. Optional: set your own `webhook_secret`. OpenShorts signs the body with HMAC-SHA256 in the `X-OpenShorts-Signature` header (`sha256=<hex>`), so you can verify the sender.\n\n### What you get back\n`event`, `job_id`, `status`, and `clips[]` with `title`, `video_url` and a 24h `download_url` per clip. Failed jobs also fire the webhook with an `error` field, so the flow never hangs.\n\nAPI docs: https://api.openshorts.app/docs \u00b7 Self-hosted works the same on your own machine (MIT).",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "note-setup",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "formTitle": "Clip a video with OpenShorts",
        "formDescription": "Paste a YouTube link (or any public video URL). You get 3-15 vertical clips with subtitles back.",
        "formFields": {
          "values": [
            {
              "fieldLabel": "Video URL",
              "requiredField": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "form-trigger",
      "name": "Video URL form",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.formTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -80,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.openshorts.app/api/process",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"url\": \"{{ $json['Video URL'] }}\",\n  \"acknowledged\": true,\n  \"webhook_url\": \"PASTE_THE_PRODUCTION_URL_OF_THE_CLIPS-READY_WEBHOOK_NODE_HERE\",\n  \"webhook_secret\": \"change-me\"\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "start-job",
      "name": "Start OpenShorts job",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        180,
        0
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "OpenShorts API key"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "job_id",
              "value": "={{ $json.job_id }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "status",
              "value": "={{ $json.status }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "job-queued",
      "name": "Job queued",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "openshorts-clips-ready",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "clips-webhook",
      "name": "Clips ready (webhook)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -80,
        320
      ],
      "webhookId": "2f8351c1-d51d-4af7-bab3-57f21e07956d"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.event }}",
              "rightValue": "job.completed",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "if-completed",
      "name": "Job completed?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        180,
        320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "fieldToSplitOut": "body.clips",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "split-clips",
      "name": "One item per clip",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitOut",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        440,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "b1",
              "name": "title",
              "value": "={{ $json.title }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "b2",
              "name": "download_url",
              "value": "={{ $json.download_url || $json.video_url }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "clip-links",
      "name": "Clip title + download link",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        700,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "e1",
              "name": "job_id",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.job_id }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "e2",
              "name": "error",
              "value": "={{ $json.body.error }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "job-failed",
      "name": "Job failed",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        440,
        420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Do something with the clips\n\nConnect *Clip title + download link* to whatever comes next: a Slack or email notification, a Google Sheet log, or post them directly via `POST /api/social/post`.\n\nEach item here is one finished 9:16 clip with subtitles burned in.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 340
      },
      "id": "note-next",
      "name": "Sticky Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        960,
        180
      ]
    }
  ],
